WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
--------------------

No source file in this repository carries a per-file copyright header. That is
a deliberate choice for a single-author codebase with a contributor agreement
(CLA.md) — headers on several hundred files add noise to every diff and drift
out of date — but it left the repository with the copyright stated nowhere at
all, which is a different problem. This file is the statement.


SECTION 13, AND WHAT YOU ARE OWED
---------------------------------

The AGPL differs from the GPL in one way that matters to anyone using a Púca
server they do not run: if you interact with this software over a network, you
are entitled to the complete corresponding source of the version that server is
running.

Every Púca server answers `GET /source` with the repository and licence of its
own build, and the app surfaces both under Settings > App Info. If you operate a
modified Púca, set SOURCE_URL to point at YOUR source, not at this repository —
otherwise you are pointing your users at code you did not run and the offer is
not satisfied.


